    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Let me create a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Summary\n\nI successfully fixed all failing tests in the frai-core suite. Here are the two issues that were resolved:\n\n### Issue 1: APPROVAL_STATUSES undefined (governance.test.js)\n**Problem:** The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./finetune/index.js`, but it was only exported in the default export object.\n\n**Fix:** Added named exports in `/packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`:\n```javascript\nexport {\n  APPROVAL_STATUSES,\n  DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS,\n  GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS,\n  RISK_LEVELS\n};\n```\n\n### Issue 2: toxicity.score returning 0 instead of 1 (eval/index.test.js)\n**Problem:** The `runEvaluations` function was calling all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but `toxicityMetric` only expects `(outputs, bannedTerms)`. This caused the references array to be passed as banned terms, incorrectly flagging legitimate outputs.\n\n**Fix:** Modified `runEvaluations` in `/packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js` to check function arity and only pass references to metrics that expect them:\n```javascript\nreturn metric.length > 1 ? metric(outs, refs) : metric(outs);\n```\n\n### Results\n- \u2705 All 8 test files passing\n- \u2705 All 28 tests passing  \n- \u2705 No breaking changes to public exports\n- \u2705 Backward compatibility maintained",
